.TH YES 1 "September 13, 2026"
.SH NAME
yes \- repeat arguments until output fails
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yes
.RI [ string ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B yes
utility repeatedly writes its arguments separated by spaces and followed by a
newline.  With zero arguments,
.B yes
writes
.BR y .
.PP
The utility reports a surfaced write failure and exits with status 1.  A
default
.B SIGPIPE
action can terminate the process before the write call returns an error.
